# Emme worksheet generated on Wed Oct 15 16:30:09 2025
# File: F:/projects/TFP/TFP2044/COB_WFH_method/build/BKR4-24-T45_TFP_network_20%WFH_50%_Errands/projects/1530to1830/Worksheets/Traffic_volumes_at_intersections.emw
#
# String Name: name of worksheet (tr,subst)
Name : PlotName
Name = Traffic volumes at intersections
# Text Description: description of worksheet (tr,subst)
Description : (0x800)
Description = <h2>Traffic volumes at intersections</h2>\
This worksheet can be used to display:\
<ul>\
<li>Turn volume as bars for <b>one</b> intersection node, with numeric values or not (layer <i>Intersection</i>).\
Predefined turn expressions are provided for the <i>Turn value</i> to display.\
By default, the size of the bars is computed automatically to a reasonable value.\
To fix the scale value, enter the desired value and keep the padlock closed (locked).\
<li>Nodes connected to the adjacent links (layer <i>Nodes</i>).\
Nodes are colored using <i>Node style</i>: first color for regular nodes, second color for centroids and third color for intersections.\
</ul>\
<b>Using this worksheet</b>\
<ul>\
<li>The initial intersection selection is set to <tt>isMarked</tt>.\
To select a specific intersection node, select from the predefined choices\
(layer <i>Intersection</i>) or from the associated <i>nodes</i> table\
(when the intersection selection is set to <tt>isMarked</tt>).\
To display one intersection node after another, \
position the mouse in the <i>Intersection node</i> input field\
and then use the up and down arrow keys.\
<li>Initially, numeric values are displayed inside the linear part of the beginning of the turn.\
To display the values outside the turn beginning and/or end, set the linear part to 0 (layer <i>Intersection</i>). \
To display numeric values even for small turn values, \
the turn offset must be at least equal to the text size.\
<li>To display values on links, enter a link value expression in the <i>Link value</i> field (layer <i>Link info</i>). \
<li>To rotate the intersection, specify the angle in degrees (layer <i>Nodes</i>). \
<li>The display of the intersection node number and of the turn table can be modified\
(layer <i>Legend</i>).\
</ul>\
<p><small>Copyright &copy; 2025, Bentley Systems, Incorporated. All rights reserved.</small>\
<p>
